# Precompile statements for the application bundle. GENERATED — do not edit by hand.
#
# `bin/trace.jl` is the execution trace and covers everything BELOW the window: loading the
# stack, building the figures, drawing into them once. It deliberately stops short of `gui()`,
# whose event loop never returns and would hang the build. So the paths that only exist when a
# real window runs — `loadqml`, the `QML.julia_call` bridge, GLMakie's `gl_convert` for our
# types — were never in the image, and were compiled on the user's first launch instead.
#
# Regenerate by unioning three traces:
#
#     julia --project=bin --trace-compile=a.trace test/gui/gui_xvfb.jl   # live window + bridge
#     julia --project=bin --trace-compile=b.trace test/gui/runtests.jl   # all four perspectives
#     julia --project=bin --trace-compile=c.trace <an engine script>     # the first-click pause
#     cat *.trace | sort -u | grep -vE '\b(Main|Test)\.' > app/precompile_statements.jl
#
# The `Main.`/`Test.` filter drops the harness's own specialisations, which have no business in
# an application. PackageCompiler is tolerant of the rest: it parses each line, skips what will
# not parse, resolves an `UndefVarError` by importing the module named, and skips what it still
# cannot resolve — so a raw trace is safe to feed.
#
# COST: every statement here is compiled INTO the image, so this trades bundle size for
# first-action latency. Both numbers are in the plan; regenerate and re-measure rather than
# assuming the trade still holds.
# already covered these, so they were never recorded; the sysimage is non-incremental and
# A second pass, from the APPLICATION's own `--trace-compile` rather than from a plain
# carries no .ji caches, so it has to compile them itself. The application's own trace is
# construction only happens with a live window.
# content are ComputePipeline's TypedEdge resolve!/set_result! and GLMakie's
# Julia process. The four traces above were collected where the packages' .ji caches
